   "t": 7.649,
   "text": "## South Australia's Daily Renewable Share (Last 30 Days)\n\n**Summary:**\nSouth Australia's renewable share over the last 30 days (19 September \u2013 18 October 2026) ranged from **51.85% to 96.16%**, with significant daily volatility:\n\n- **Highest:** 96.16% on 20 September\n- **Lowest:** 51.85% on 1 October\n- **Average:** ~77.5% (typical for SA1, which has substantial wind and solar capacity)\n\n**Key observations:**\n- The share fluctuates considerably day-to-day, reflecting variable wind and solar generation\n- Several days exceeded 85% renewable penetration (20, 27, 28, 29 Sept; 8, 9, 10, 12 Oct)\n- Dips below 60% occurred on 1, 4, 5 October, likely due to lower wind/solar output and higher demand\n- No clear upward or downward trend over the 30-day period\u2014the variation is driven by weather and demand patterns\n\n**Tool used:** `query_cube` on the `renewable_share` cube, filtered to SA1 region with daily granularity over the last 30 days.",
